 "narrative": "## The trajectory\nRevenue was $184.4B in FY2025 [1].\nRevenue CAGR was +5.4% over FY2016..FY2025 [2].\nNet income was $12.3B in FY2025 [3].\n\n## Growth quality\nRevenue growth in FY2025 was -4.6% [1] [4].\nNet income growth in FY2025 was -30.5% [3] [5].\nIn FY2025, operating cash flow growth of +7.8% [6] [7] was above net income growth of -30.5% [3] [5].\n\n## Margins\nNet margin was 6.7% in FY2025 [8].\nNet margin changed -2.5pp in FY2025 [8] [9].\n\n## Cash & balance sheet\nIn FY2025, free cash flow of $16.6B [10] was above net income of $12.3B [3].\nThe current ratio was 1.15\u00d7 in FY2025 [11], above 1.00\u00d7.\nIn FY2025, operating cash flow of $33.9B [6] was above net income of $12.3B [3].\n\n## Red flags\nNet margin compressed 4.2pp over three periods: 10.9% \u2192 9.2% \u2192 6.7%. Source operands: Net margin 10.9% in FY2023 [12]; Net margin 9.2% in FY2024 [9]; Net margin 6.7% in FY2025 [8].\n\n## What to watch next\nWatch whether revenue growth in the next reporting update improves from -4.6% in FY2025 [1] [4].\nWatch how net income in the next reporting update compares with $12.3B in FY2025 [3].\nWatch how free cash flow in the next reporting update compares with $16.6B in FY2025 [10].",
